# scene_loader — every bug this target has found, pinned forever.
# One decimal master seed per line; `--seed <n>` reproduces one exactly.
# See tests/fuzz/corpus/README.md for the lane contract.

# ── Truncation accepted as success ───────────────────────────────────────────
# loadScene ended in `return f.good() || f.eof()`, so a short read succeeded:
# the header still claimed the original counts while the tail came back
# zero-filled, indistinguishable from real content. An interrupted cook or a
# partial download loaded as a valid scene.
2277151743773813066
6965110661002779539

# ── Unbounded allocation from a 32-byte header ───────────────────────────────
# entityCount and stringTableSize were resize()d straight from the header:
# 2.7 GB requested from a 3 482-byte file, and 0xFFFFFFFF entities asks for
# 1 TB. A 20-iteration explore run was SIGKILLed by the OOM killer.
16861278626067538202

# ── stringTableRead: offset+length wrapped in 32-bit ─────────────────────────
# The bound was `offset + length > table.size()`, computed in 32-bit because
# both fields are uint32_t. offset=0xFFFFFFF0 with length=0x20 wraps to 0x10,
# passes the check, and builds a std::string from a pointer 4 GB past the
# buffer. Reproduced here as an 88-byte read from offset 4294967234 in a
# 32-byte table — a heap overread from nothing but a corrupt cooked scene.
12348081055662259564
14935072500733692310
6035412806354011894
